nside functions or methods\n- **Type hints required** — All fields and methods must have proper type hints\n- **Always use absolute imports** — relative `..` imports break in UAC zip loading (e.g., `from exceptions import ...`, NOT `from ..exceptions import ...`)\n\n## Remote Filesystem Access\n\nUAC executes tasks on remote agent machines — these are separate systems that you have absolutely no access to. When a task runs, the UAC Controller dispatches it to the selected agent host, which runs the extension process on that machine. You cannot read, verify, list, or reason about any files, directories, paths, or output files on the agent host. All information available to you comes exclusively through the issue logs and extension source code provided in the prompt. Do not attempt to access or infer anything about the remote filesystem.\n\n# Tasks\n\nUse the `Task` Tools to manage the flow of the execution.\nWhen creating the Task Definitions creat it with this metadology:\n\n```\n<Agent Name>: <Task Name>\n```\n\n## Task 1: Read Issue Logs\n\nRead all **Input Files** listed in the prompt.\n\n## Task 2: Gather Context\n\nRead all remaining **Input Files** listed in the prompt (the extension source files).\n\nUse `ue-ca:retrieving-context` skill to read implementation best practices:\n- `references/implementation_docs/actions.md` — Action patterns and error handling\n- `references/implementation_docs/action_output.md` — ActionOutput dataclass patterns\n- `references/implementation_docs/exceptions.md` — Exception handling\n- `references/implementation_docs/input_fields.md` — Input field patterns\n- `references/implementation_docs/logging.md` — Logging patterns\n- `references/implementation_docs/manager.md` — ExtensionManager usage\n\n## Task 3: Validate Fixes Against Analysis\n\nFor each planned fix, verify it is consistent with `memory/analysis.md` before touching any code:\n\n- **Implementation error** — a code-level mistake (wrong field name, unhandled exception, incorrect parsing, wrong API call) that does not require changing the extension's design → **proceed with fix**\n- **Design gap** — the fix would require adding, removing, or changing an action, field, auth method, or core behavior that the analysis defines — this is not a bug, it is a missing or incorrect implementation → **mark as unresolved**, do not patch\n\nIf a fix is valid, confirm it does not:\n- Add or remove actions, fields, or auth methods not described in the analysis\n- Change the extension's public interface or expected outputs\n- Introduce behaviour the analysis does not account for\n\nAny fix that fails this check must be left unresolved with a note explaining why it diverges from the analysis.\n\n## Task 4: Apply Fixes\n\nFor each issue log that passed Task 3 validation:\n\n1. Identify the affected file(s) listed under `### Affected Files`\n2. Read the current content of each affected file\n3. Apply the minimal change needed to address the root cause — do NOT change unrelated code\n4. If an issue cannot be confidently fixed (e.g., requires external service knowledge), skip it and note it as unresolved\n\n## Task 5: Validate\n\n## Task: Validate Imports\n\n**Third-party imports** — verify each import path exists in the virtual environment:\n\n```bash\nls /tmp/ue-3-aws-object-storage/ue-dev-env/lib/python*/site-packages/[package_name]/\ngrep -n \"class ClassName\\|def function_name\" /tmp/ue-3-aws-object-storage/ue-dev-env/lib/python*/site-packages/[package_name]/[module].py\n```\n\nNever assume import paths from documentation, verify against the actual installed package.\n\n**Extension imports** — verify every name imported from extension modules actually exists in the source:\n\n```bash\ngrep -rn \"^from exceptions import\\|^from fields\\|^from actions import\\|^from utility\" src/\n```\n\nCross-check each imported name against the corresponding source file to confirm it is defined.\n\nFix any mismatches before proceeding.\n\n## Task: Validate Python 